dante 1.4.4 libdsocks: numeric IPv6 addresses in getaddrinfo(3) with
resolveprotocol: fake

Applies on top of the other dante-*.patch files (it only touches
Rgetaddrinfo() in lib/Rgethostbyname.c).

With "resolveprotocol: fake", Rgetaddrinfo() passes numeric addresses to
the system getaddrinfo() (only names are faked), but it forced
ai_family = AF_INET for them. getaddrinfo("::") or ("::1") therefore
failed, so a preloaded program could not resolve an IPv6 literal, e.g. to
listen on "::". The numeric-address check also tested ai_protocol instead
of ai_family, and with a family in the hints only tried that family: with
ai_protocol set (e.g. IPPROTO_TCP) and AF_UNSPEC it returned fake IPv4
addresses for "::" and even for "127.0.0.1", and "::" asked for as AF_INET
was faked instead of failing.

Numeric addresses (of either family) now go to getaddrinfo() with the
caller's family (and AI_NUMERICHOST, so no DNS lookup happens). Names are
still faked, as IPv4. This does not make
IPv6 sockets socksified: a program that connects to an IPv6 literal
connects directly.

Test: test/gaicheck.c (via test/run.sh).

--- a/lib/Rgethostbyname.c
+++ b/lib/Rgethostbyname.c
@@ -225,21 +225,18 @@
 
    SASSERTX(nodename != NULL);
 
-   if (hints == NULL || hints->ai_protocol == PF_UNSPEC) {
-      if (socks_inet_pton(AF_INET,  nodename, addrbuf, NULL) == 1
-      ||  socks_inet_pton(AF_INET6, nodename, addrbuf, NULL) == 1)
-         isipaddr = 1;
-      else
-         isipaddr = 0;
-   }
-   else {
-      SASSERTX(hints != NULL);
-
-      if (socks_inet_pton(hints->ai_family, nodename, addrbuf, NULL) == 1)
-         isipaddr = 1;
-      else
-         isipaddr = 0;
-   }
+   /*
+    * Either family, whatever hints->ai_family says: an IPv6 literal asked
+    * for as AF_INET must fail in getaddrinfo() below, not be faked as a
+    * name.  (This tested hints->ai_protocol == PF_UNSPEC and otherwise only
+    * hints->ai_family, so e.g. "::" or "127.0.0.1" with IPPROTO_TCP and
+    * AF_UNSPEC were faked.)
+    */
+   if (socks_inet_pton(AF_INET,  nodename, addrbuf, NULL) == 1
+   ||  socks_inet_pton(AF_INET6, nodename, addrbuf, NULL) == 1)
+      isipaddr = 1;
+   else
+      isipaddr = 0;
 
    if (isipaddr) {
       fakeip_cantry = 0;
@@ -275,7 +272,12 @@
 
             /*
              * With AI_NUMERICHOST this should not result in any DNS lookup.
+             * Keep the caller's family: an IPv6 literal (e.g., "::" for a
+             * listening socket) is not something we fake, and forcing
+             * AF_INET made getaddrinfo() fail for it.  Only names are
+             * faked, and those always as IPv4.
              */
+            fakehints.ai_family = hints == NULL ? AF_UNSPEC : hints->ai_family;
             gaierr = getaddrinfo(nodename, servname, &fakehints, res);
 
             slog(LOG_DEBUG, "%s: getaddrinfo(%s, %s) returned %d (%s)",
